* Typing ``lvalue``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``:
* The result is ``typedLvalueIR``.

xref:Lvalue_ok[Typing ``prefixedNonTypeName``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``]:

. Let ``prefixedNameIR`` be xref:prefixedNonTypeName[the prefixed name of  ``prefixedNonTypeName``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
. Let ``direction`` ``typeIR`` ``ctk`` ``value^?^`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:find_var_t[the type of variable ``prefixedNameIR`` from the ``p`` layer of ``TC``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
. Check that ``ctk`` is ``+DYN+``.
. Check that ``value^?^`` is none.
. Check that ``direction`` is equal to ``+OUT+`` or ``direction`` is equal to ``+INOUT+``.
. The result is xref:typedLvalueIR[``prefixedNameIR`` with note ``+`(+`` ``typeIR`` ``+`)+``].

xref:Lvalue_ok[Typing ``lvalue~base~`` ``+'.'+`` ``member``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``]:

. Let ``typedLvalueIR~base~`` be the result of xref:Lvalue_ok[typing ``lvalue~base~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
