. Let ``typeIR'`` be xref:unroll_typeIR[``typeIR~base~`` with typedefs unrolled].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
. If let ``+HEADER_STACK+`` ``typeIR`` ``+`[+`` ``++_++`` ``+`]+`` be ``typeIR'``:
 .. Let ``nameIR`` be xref:name[the name of ``member``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Check that ``nameIR`` is equal to ``"next"`` or ``nameIR`` is equal to ``"last"``.
 .. Check that ``p`` is equal to ``+BLOCK+`` and ``TC.+BLOCK+.+KIND+`` is equal to ``+PARSER+`` or ``p`` is equal to ``+LOCAL+`` and ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+`` is equal to ``+PARSER_STATE+``.
 .. Let ``typedLvalueIR`` be xref:typedLvalueIR[``typedLvalueIR~base~`` ``+'.'+`` ``nameIR`` with note ``+`(+`` ``typeIR`` ``+`)+``].
 .. The result is ``typedLvalueIR``.
. Else if let ``+STRUCT+`` ``++_++`` ``+`<+`` ``++_++^{asterisk}^`` ``+`>+`` ``+`{+`` ``(`` ``++_++`` ``typeIR~field~`` ``nameIR~field~`` ``+';'+`` ``)^{asterisk}^`` ``+`}+`` be ``typeIR'``:
 .. Let ``nameIR`` be xref:name[the name of ``member``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``typeIR`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:assoc_[the value associated to ``nameIR`` in ``(`` ``nameIR~field~,`` ``typeIR~field~`` ``)^{asterisk}^``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``typedLvalueIR`` be xref:typedLvalueIR[``typedLvalueIR~base~`` ``+'.'+`` ``nameIR`` with note ``+`(+`` ``typeIR`` ``+`)+``].
 .. The result is ``typedLvalueIR``.
. Else if let ``+HEADER+`` ``++_++`` ``+`<+`` ``++_++^{asterisk}^`` ``+`>+`` ``+`{+`` ``(`` ``++_++`` ``typeIR~field~`` ``nameIR~field~`` ``+';'+`` ``)^{asterisk}^`` ``+`}+`` be ``typeIR'``:
 .. Let ``nameIR`` be xref:name[the name of ``member``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``typeIR`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:assoc_[the value associated to ``nameIR`` in ``(`` ``nameIR~field~,`` ``typeIR~field~`` ``)^{asterisk}^``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``typedLvalueIR`` be xref:typedLvalueIR[``typedLvalueIR~base~`` ``+'.'+`` ``nameIR`` with note ``+`(+`` ``typeIR`` ``+`)+``].
 .. The result is ``typedLvalueIR``.
. Else if let ``+HEADER_UNION+`` ``++_++`` ``+`<+`` ``++_++^{asterisk}^`` ``+`>+`` ``+`{+`` ``(`` ``++_++`` ``typeIR~field~`` ``nameIR~field~`` ``+';'+`` ``)^{asterisk}^`` ``+`}+`` be ``typeIR'``:
 .. Let ``nameIR`` be xref:name[the name of ``member``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``typeIR`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:assoc_[the value associated to ``nameIR`` in ``(`` ``nameIR~field~,`` ``typeIR~field~`` ``)^{asterisk}^``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``typedLvalueIR`` be xref:typedLvalueIR[``typedLvalueIR~base~`` ``+'.'+`` ``nameIR`` with note ``+`(+`` ``typeIR`` ``+`)+``].
 .. The result is ``typedLvalueIR``.

<<Lvalue_ok,Typing ``lvalue~base~`` ``+`[+`` ``expression~index~`` ``+`]+``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``>>:

. Let ``typedLvalueIR~base~`` be the result of xref:Lvalue_ok[typing ``lvalue~base~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
. Let ``+`(+`` ``typeIR~base~`` ``+`)+`` be the note of ``typedLvalueIR~base~``.
. Let ``typeIR'`` be xref:unroll_typeIR[``typeIR~base~`` with typedefs unrolled].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
. If let ``+ARRAY+`` ``typeIR`` ``+`[+`` ``n~size~`` ``+`]+`` be ``typeIR'``:
 .. Let ``typedExpressionIR~index~`` be the result of xref:Expr_ok[typing ``expression~index~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let xref:expressionNoteIR[a pair of type ``typeIR~index~`` and compile-time known-ness ``ctk~index~``] be the note of ``typedExpressionIR~index~``.
 .. Let ``typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:reduce_serenum_unary[the result of reducing serializable enums in ``typedExpressionIR~index~`` until ``$compat_array_index`` is satisfied].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. If ``ctk~index~`` is ``+LCTK+``:
  ... Let ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
  ... Let!~type~ ``integerValue~index~`` be ``value``.+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
  ... Let ``n~index~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:nat_of_integerValue[the natural number representation of  ``integerValue~index~``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
  ... Check that ``n~index~`` is less than ``n~size~``.
  ... Let ``typedLvalueIR`` be <<typedLvalueIR,``typedLvalueIR~base~`` ``+`[+`` ``typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~`` ``+`]+`` with note ``+`(+`` ``typeIR`` ``+`)+``>>.
  ... The result is ``typedLvalueIR``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``typedLvalueIR`` be <<typedLvalueIR,``typedLvalueIR~base~`` ``+`[+`` ``typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~`` ``+`]+`` with note ``+`(+`` ``typeIR`` ``+`)+``>>.
  ... The result is ``typedLvalueIR``.
. Else if let ``+HEADER_STACK+`` ``typeIR`` ``+`[+`` ``n~size~`` ``+`]+`` be ``typeIR'``:
 .. Let ``typedExpressionIR~index~`` be the result of xref:Expr_ok[typing ``expression~index~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let xref:expressionNoteIR[a pair of type ``typeIR~index~`` and compile-time known-ness ``ctk~index~``] be the note of ``typedExpressionIR~index~``.
 .. Let ``typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:reduce_serenum_unary[the result of reducing serializable enums in ``typedExpressionIR~index~`` until ``$compat_array_index`` is satisfied].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. If ``ctk~index~`` is ``+LCTK+``:
  ... Let ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
  ... Let!~type~ ``integerValue~index~`` be ``value``.+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
  ... Let ``n~index~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:nat_of_integerValue[the natural number representation of  ``integerValue~index~``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
  ... Check that ``n~index~`` is less than ``n~size~``.
  ... Let ``typedLvalueIR`` be <<typedLvalueIR,``typedLvalueIR~base~`` ``+`[+`` ``typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~`` ``+`]+`` with note ``+`(+`` ``typeIR`` ``+`)+``>>.
  ... The result is ``typedLvalueIR``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``typedLvalueIR`` be <<typedLvalueIR,``typedLvalueIR~base~`` ``+`[+`` ``typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~`` ``+`]+`` with note ``+`(+`` ``typeIR`` ``+`)+``>>.
