<<Lvalue_ok,Typing ``lvalue~base~`` ``+`[+`` ``expression`` ``sliceop`` ``expression'`` ``+`]+``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``>>:

. If ``sliceop`` matches pattern ``+':'+``:
 .. Let ``typedLvalueIR~base~`` be the result of xref:Lvalue_ok[typing ``lvalue~base~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let ``+`(+`` ``typeIR~base~`` ``+`)+`` be the note of ``typedLvalueIR~base~``.
 .. Check that xref:compat_bitslice_base[``typeIR~base~`` can be used as a bitslice base].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``typedExpressionIR~hi~`` be the result of xref:Expr_ok[typing ``expression``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let ``typedExpressionIR~lo~`` be the result of xref:Expr_ok[typing ``expression'``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let ``typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:reduce_serenum_unary[the result of reducing serializable enums in ``typedExpressionIR~hi~`` until ``$compat_bitslice_range_index`` is satisfied].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:reduce_serenum_unary[the result of reducing serializable enums in ``typedExpressionIR~lo~`` until ``$compat_bitslice_range_index`` is satisfied].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let xref:expressionNoteIR[a pair of type ``typeIR~hi_reduced~`` and compile-time known-ness ``ctk~hi_reduced~``] be the note of ``typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~``.
 .. Let xref:expressionNoteIR[a pair of type ``typeIR~lo_reduced~`` and compile-time known-ness ``ctk~lo_reduced~``] be the note of ``typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~``.
 .. Check that ``ctk~hi_reduced~`` is ``+LCTK+``.
 .. Let ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``integerValue~hi~`` be ``value``.+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``n~hi~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:nat_of_integerValue[the natural number representation of  ``integerValue~hi~``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Check that ``ctk~lo_reduced~`` is ``+LCTK+``.
 .. Let ``value'`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``integerValue~lo~`` be ``value'``.+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``n~lo~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:nat_of_integerValue[the natural number representation of  ``integerValue~lo~``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Check that <<is_valid_bitslice,``typeIR~base~`` ``+`[+`` ``n~lo~`` ``+':'+`` ``n~hi~`` ``+`]+`` is a valid bitslice>>.+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``i`` be ``n~hi~`` ``-`` ``n~lo~`` ``{plus}`` ``1``.
 .. Let!~type~ ``n~slice~`` be ``i``.+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``typeIR`` be ``+BIT+`` ``+`<+`` ``n~slice~`` ``+`>+``.
 .. Let ``typedLvalueIR`` be <<typedLvalueIR,``typedLvalueIR~base~`` ``+`[+`` ``typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~`` ``+':'+`` ``typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~`` ``+`]+`` with note ``+`(+`` ``typeIR`` ``+`)+``>>.
 .. The result is ``typedLvalueIR``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``typedLvalueIR~base~`` be the result of xref:Lvalue_ok[typing ``lvalue~base~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let ``+`(+`` ``typeIR~base~`` ``+`)+`` be the note of ``typedLvalueIR~base~``.
 .. Check that xref:compat_bitslice_base[``typeIR~base~`` can be used as a bitslice base].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``typedExpressionIR~l~`` be the result of xref:Expr_ok[typing ``expression``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let ``typedExpressionIR~w~`` be the result of xref:Expr_ok[typing ``expression'``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let ``typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:reduce_serenum_unary[the result of reducing serializable enums in ``typedExpressionIR~l~`` until ``$compat_bitslice_offset_index`` is satisfied].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``typedExpressionIR~w_reduced~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:reduce_serenum_unary[the result of reducing serializable enums in ``typedExpressionIR~w~`` until ``$compat_bitslice_offset_width`` is satisfied].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let xref:expressionNoteIR[a pair of type ``typeIR~w_reduced~`` and compile-time known-ness ``ctk~w_reduced~``] be the note of ``typedExpressionIR~w_reduced~``.
 .. Check that ``ctk~w_reduced~`` is ``+LCTK+``.
 .. Let ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~w_reduced~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``integerValue~w~`` be ``value``.+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``n~w~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:nat_of_integerValue[the natural number representation of  ``integerValue~w~``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[FAIL]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``typeIR`` be ``+BIT+`` ``+`<+`` ``n~w~`` ``+`>+``.
 .. Let ``typedLvalueIR`` be <<typedLvalueIR,``typedLvalueIR~base~`` ``+`[+`` ``typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`` ``{apos}{plus}:{apos}`` ``typedExpressionIR~w_reduced~`` ``+`]+`` with note ``+`(+`` ``typeIR`` ``+`)+``>>.
 .. The result is ``typedLvalueIR``.

xref:Lvalue_ok[Typing ``+`(+`` ``lvalue~base~`` ``+`)+``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``]:

. Let ``typedLvalueIR~base~`` be the result of xref:Lvalue_ok[typing ``lvalue~base~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
. Let ``+`(+`` ``typeIR~base~`` ``+`)+`` be the note of ``typedLvalueIR~base~``.
. Let ``typedLvalueIR`` be xref:typedLvalueIR[``+`(+`` ``typedLvalueIR~base~`` ``+`)+`` with note ``+`(+`` ``typeIR~base~`` ``+`)+``].
. The result is ``typedLvalueIR``.

Lvalue_ok dispatch:

. If let ``prefixedNonTypeName`` be ``lvalue``: goto xref:Lvalue_ok-referenceExpression[referenceExpression]
. Else if let ``lvalue~base~`` ``+'.'+`` ``member`` be ``lvalue``: goto xref:Lvalue_ok-memberAccess[memberAccess]
. Else if let ``lvalue~base~`` ``+`[+`` ``expression~index~`` ``+`]+`` be ``lvalue``: goto xref:Lvalue_ok-indexAccess[indexAccess]
. Else if let ``lvalue~base~`` ``+`[+`` ``expression`` ``sliceop`` ``expression'`` ``+`]+`` be ``lvalue``: goto xref:Lvalue_ok-sliceAccess[sliceAccess]
. Else if let ``+`(+`` ``lvalue~base~`` ``+`)+`` be ``lvalue``: goto xref:Lvalue_ok-parenthesized[parenthesized]

xref:Stmt_ok[Stmt_ok]:

* Typing ``statement``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``:
* The result is context ``TC`` and ``statementIR``.

xref:Stmt_ok[Typing ``+';'+``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``]:

. The result is context ``TC`` and ``+';'+``.

xref:Stmt_ok[Typing ``lvalue`` ``assignop`` ``expression`` ``+';'+``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``]:

. If ``assignop`` is ``+'='+``:
 .. Let ``typedLvalueIR`` be the result of xref:Lvalue_ok[typing ``lvalue``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let ``typedExpressionIR`` be the result of xref:Expr_ok[typing ``expression``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let ``typeIR~l~`` be xref:type_of_typedLvalueIR[the type of lvalue ``typedLvalueIR``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[<a href="#Stmt_ok-returnStatement">→ returnStatement</a>]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``typeIR~r~`` be xref:type_of_typedExpressionIR[the type of ``typedExpressionIR``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[<a href="#Stmt_ok-returnStatement">→ returnStatement</a>]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``typedExpressionIR~cast~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:cast_unary[``typedExpressionIR`` implicitly cast to ``typeIR~l~``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[<a href="#Stmt_ok-returnStatement">→ returnStatement</a>]</sub>+++
 .. The result is context ``TC`` and ``typedLvalueIR`` ``+'='+`` ``typedExpressionIR~cast~`` ``+';'+``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``binop`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:assignop_as_binop[the binary operator corresponding to ``assignop``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[<a href="#Stmt_ok-returnStatement">→ returnStatement</a>]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``typedLvalueIR`` be the result of xref:Lvalue_ok[typing ``lvalue``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let ``expression~lvalue~`` be xref:lvalue_as_expression[the expression corresponding to ``lvalue``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[<a href="#Stmt_ok-returnStatement">→ returnStatement</a>]</sub>+++
 .. Let ``expression~binary~`` be ``expression~lvalue~`` ``binop`` ``expression``.
 .. Let ``typedExpressionIR~binary~`` be the result of xref:Expr_ok[typing ``expression~binary~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let ``+`(+`` ``typeIR~lvalue~`` ``+`)+`` be the note of ``typedLvalueIR``.
 .. Let ``expressionIR`` ``+'#'+`` ``++_++`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:cast_unary[``typedExpressionIR~binary~`` implicitly cast to ``typeIR~lvalue~``].+++<sub class="bk-mark">[<a href="#Stmt_ok-returnStatement">→ returnStatement</a>]</sub>+++
 .. Let!~type~ ``++_++`` ``binop''`` ``typedExpressionIR~cast~`` be ``expressionIR``.+++<sub class="bk-mark">[<a href="#Stmt_ok-returnStatement">→ returnStatement</a>]</sub>+++
 .. Check that ``binop''`` is equal to ``binop``.
 .. The result is context ``TC`` and ``typedLvalueIR`` ``assignop`` ``typedExpressionIR~cast~`` ``+';'+``.

xref:Stmt_ok[Typing ``callStatement``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``]:

. If let ``lvalue~callable~`` ``+`(+`` ``argumentList`` ``+`)+`` ``+';'+`` be ``callStatement``:
 .. Let typed callable target ``callableTargetIR`` be the result of xref:CallableTarget_lvalue_ok[typing ``lvalue~callable~`` as a callable target, under cursor ``p`` and context ``TC``].
 .. Let ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:ArgumentList_ok[typing ``argumentList``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let callable type ``callableTypeIR`` with fresh type variables ``typeId~impl~^{asterisk}^``, defaults ``id~default~^{asterisk}^`` and optionals ``id~optional~^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:CallableType_ok[finding type of callable call ``callableTargetIR`` ``+`<+`` ``·`` ``+`>+`` ``+`(+`` ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+`)+``, under cursor ``p`` and context ``TC``].
 .. Let ``typeArgumentIR~infer~^{asterisk}^`` be ``(`` ``{nbsp}~NAME~`` ``typeId~impl~`` ``)^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Let return type ``typeIR~ret~`` with inferred ``typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`` and casted ``argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:Call_ok[typing invocation ``callableTypeIR`` ``+`<+`` ``typeArgumentIR~infer~^{asterisk}^`` ``+`>+`` ``+`(+`` ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+`)+`` with omitted type arguments ``typeId~impl~^{asterisk}^``, defaults ``id~default~^{asterisk}^`` and optionals ``id~optional~^{asterisk}^``, under cursor ``p`` and context ``TC``].
 .. If xref:is_static_assert_callableTypeIR[``callableTypeIR`` is a static_assert call]:+++<sub class="bk-mark">[<a href="#Stmt_ok-returnStatement">→ returnStatement</a>]</sub>+++
  ... Let ``callExpressionIR`` be ``callableTargetIR`` ``+`<+`` ``typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`` ``+`>+`` ``+`(+`` ``argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`` ``+`)+``.
  ... Let ``expressionNoteIR`` be xref:expressionNoteIR[a pair of type ``typeIR~ret~`` and compile-time known-ness ``+LCTK+``].
  ... Let ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``callExpressionIR`` annotated with ``expressionNoteIR``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
  ... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``{nbsp}~B~`` ``true``.
  ... Let ``emptyStatementIR`` be ``+';'+``.
  ... The result is context ``TC`` and ``emptyStatementIR``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``callStatementIR`` be ``callableTargetIR`` ``+`<+`` ``typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`` ``+`>+`` ``+`(+`` ``argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`` ``+`)+`` ``+';'+``.
  ... The result is context ``TC`` and ``callStatementIR``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``lvalue~callable~`` ``+`<+`` ``typeArgumentList`` ``+`>+`` ``+`(+`` ``argumentList`` ``+`)+`` ``+';'+`` be ``callStatement``.
 .. Let typed callable target ``callableTargetIR`` be the result of xref:CallableTarget_lvalue_ok[typing ``lvalue~callable~`` as a callable target, under cursor ``p`` and context ``TC``].
 .. Let ``typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^`` and fresh type variables ``typeId~impl~^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:TypeArgumentList_ok[typing ``typeArgumentList``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:ArgumentList_ok[typing ``argumentList``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
 .. Let callable type ``callableTypeIR`` with fresh type variables ``typeId~inserted~^{asterisk}^``, defaults ``id~default~^{asterisk}^`` and optionals ``id~optional~^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:CallableType_ok[finding type of callable call ``callableTargetIR`` ``+`<+`` ``typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+`>+`` ``+`(+`` ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+`)+``, under cursor ``p`` and context ``TC``].
 .. Let ``typeArgumentIR~infer~^{asterisk}^`` be ``typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^`` concatenated with ``(`` ``{nbsp}~NAME~`` ``typeId~inserted~`` ``)^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Let ``typeId~infer~^{asterisk}^`` be ``typeId~impl~^{asterisk}^`` concatenated with ``typeId~inserted~^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Let return type ``typeIR~ret~`` with inferred ``typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`` and casted ``argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:Call_ok[typing invocation ``callableTypeIR`` ``+`<+`` ``typeArgumentIR~infer~^{asterisk}^`` ``+`>+`` ``+`(+`` ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+`)+`` with omitted type arguments ``typeId~infer~^{asterisk}^``, defaults ``id~default~^{asterisk}^`` and optionals ``id~optional~^{asterisk}^``, under cursor ``p`` and context ``TC``].
 .. Let ``callStatementIR`` be ``callableTargetIR`` ``+`<+`` ``typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`` ``+`>+`` ``+`(+`` ``argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`` ``+`)+`` ``+';'+``.
 .. The result is context ``TC`` and ``callStatementIR``.

xref:Stmt_ok[Typing ``namedType`` ``+'.'+`` ``+APPLY+`` ``+`(+`` ``argumentList`` ``+`)+`` ``+';'+``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``]:

. Let ``expressionIR`` annotated with a pair of type ``typeIR~object~`` and compile-time known-ness ``++_++`` be the result of xref:Expr_ok[typing ``namedType`` ``+`(+`` ``{nbsp}~EMPTY~`` ``+`)+``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
. Let!~type~ ``callExpressionIR`` be ``expressionIR``.+++<sub class="bk-mark">[<a href="#Stmt_ok-returnStatement">→ returnStatement</a>]</sub>+++
