<<is_valid_bitslice,``typeIR'`` ``+`[+`` ``n~lo~`` ``+':'+`` ``n~hi~`` ``+`]+`` is a valid bitslice>>

. If let ``intTypeIR`` be ``typeIR'``:
 .. Return ``n~lo~`` is less than or equal to ``n~hi~``.
. Else if let ``+INT+`` ``+`<+`` ``w`` ``+`>+`` be ``typeIR'``:
 .. Let ``i`` be ``n~hi~`` ``-`` ``n~lo~`` ``{plus}`` ``1``.
 .. Let!~type~ ``w~slice~`` be ``i``.+++<sub class="bk-mark">[<a href="#is_valid_bitslice-else">→ ⋅</a>]</sub>+++
 .. Return ``n~lo~`` is less than or equal to ``n~hi~`` and ``n~hi~`` is less than or equal to ``w`` and ``w~slice~`` is less than or equal to ``w``.
. Else if let ``+BIT+`` ``+`<+`` ``w`` ``+`>+`` be ``typeIR'``:
 .. Let ``i`` be ``n~hi~`` ``-`` ``n~lo~`` ``{plus}`` ``1``.
 .. Let!~type~ ``w~slice~`` be ``i``.+++<sub class="bk-mark">[<a href="#is_valid_bitslice-else">→ ⋅</a>]</sub>+++
 .. Return ``n~lo~`` is less than or equal to ``n~hi~`` and ``n~hi~`` is less than or equal to ``w`` and ``w~slice~`` is less than or equal to ``w``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``+TYPEDEF+`` ``++_++`` ``typeIR`` be ``typeIR'``.
 .. Return <<is_valid_bitslice,``typeIR`` ``+`[+`` ``n~lo~`` ``+':'+`` ``n~hi~`` ``+`]+`` is a valid bitslice>>.+++<sub class="bk-mark">[<a href="#is_valid_bitslice-else">→ ⋅</a>]</sub>+++

. +++<span id="is_valid_bitslice-else"></span>+++Otherwise: return ``false``.

